  "title": "Piri Reis",
  "summary": "Piri Reis was an Ottoman admiral, geographer and cartographer, born between 1465 and 1470 in Gallipoli, who began his sea career under his uncle Kemal Reis. After 1511 he returned to Gallipoli and compiled a world map in 1513, found in Topkapi Palace in 1929, and later wrote the sailing manual Kitab-i Bahriye. He died in 1554 or 1555.",
